DTSTAMP:20260924T122623Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20250421
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20250422
SUMMARY:New Jersey: State sales & use tax return due
DESCRIPTION:Quarterly is the standard filing frequency\, due 20th of month 
 following the quarter end (larger filers make monthly prepayments in betwee
 n). | Q1 2026 (Jan-Mar) sales tax return\, applying New Jersey's quarterly-
 filer due-date rule: Quarterly is the standard filing frequency\, due 20th 
 of month following the quarter end (larger filers make monthly prepayments 
 in between). This is a representative recurring pattern\, not a single annu
 al deadline - actual filing frequency (monthly/quarterly/annual) is assigne
 d per business by the state. | Authority: Direct fetch of New Jersey's own 
 tax agency site this session | Source: https://www.nj.gov/treasury/taxation
 /sales-use-filing.shtml | This date is computed from a recurrence rule and 
 may not reflect a later-announced change\; confirm against the cited source
  before relying on it.
